WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.545
Inferences

00:00:01.925 --> 00:00:04.587
Pick what MUST be true, not what COULD be.

00:00:05.787 --> 00:00:06.785
How to spot it

00:00:07.185 --> 00:00:08.982
A passage that ends in a blank

00:00:09.532 --> 00:00:12.688
The question says “most logically completes the text”

00:00:13.238 --> 00:00:17.619
It’s testing: logic: what the evidence actually proves

00:00:18.819 --> 00:00:19.614
The method

00:00:20.014 --> 00:00:22.731
Step 1: Paraphrase each sentence

00:00:23.011 --> 00:00:24.208
A few words each.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.204
Step 2: Find the key evidence

00:00:27.484 --> 00:00:30.019
A surprise, or two facts to combine.

00:00:30.569 --> 00:00:33.008
Step 3: Predict the conclusion

00:00:33.288 --> 00:00:34.769
If A and B, then…

00:00:35.319 --> 00:00:37.415
Step 4: Cut “could be true”

00:00:37.695 --> 00:00:39.106
And anything too strong.

00:00:39.656 --> 00:00:40.766
In a few words

00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:43.690
Evidence. Predict. Must be true.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:45.956
Logic rules

00:00:46.356 --> 00:00:48.187
Must be true beats could be true

00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:49.878
Combine the facts

00:00:50.158 --> 00:00:52.161
The answer usually links two of them.

00:00:52.711 --> 00:00:54.101
Watch the small words

00:00:54.381 --> 00:00:56.807
only, unlike, before, most

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.860
Modest beats extreme

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.361
“May have contributed” beats “caused all”.

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:03.601
Let’s try one

00:01:04.001 --> 00:01:10.012
Archaeologists excavating a 9,000-year-old village found seeds of wild barley in the oldest layers

00:01:10.012 --> 00:01:17.635
of soil. In layers dating to about 500 years later, they found barley seeds with tough stems that

00:01:17.635 --> 00:01:24.150
do not shatter and scatter seeds on their own, a trait that appears only when people repeatedly harvest

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.319
and replant a crop. These findings suggest that ______

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:31.429
Which choice most logically completes the text?

00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:35.460
Fact one: the oldest layers have wild barley.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:41.194
Fact two: later layers show a trait that appears only when people farm barley.

00:01:41.744 --> 00:01:49.409
Combine them: farming started in between. Nothing in the text proves A, B, or D. Choice C.

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:51.605
Common traps

00:01:52.005 --> 00:01:52.902
Could be true

00:01:53.182 --> 00:01:55.468
Sounds smart. Never proven.

00:01:56.018 --> 00:01:56.850
Reversal

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.807
Gets the direction backwards.

00:02:00.007 --> 00:02:00.952
Inferences

00:02:01.232 --> 00:02:04.006
Evidence. Predict. Must be true.

00:02:04.556 --> 00:02:05.329
Spot it

00:02:05.529 --> 00:02:09.339
Passage ends in a blank: “most logically completes”

00:02:09.889 --> 00:02:10.596
Steps

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:12.965
1. Paraphrase each sentence

00:02:13.245 --> 00:02:15.212
2. Find the key evidence

00:02:15.492 --> 00:02:17.448
3. Predict the conclusion

00:02:17.728 --> 00:02:20.010
4. Cut could-be-true and too-strong

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.313
Remember

00:02:21.513 --> 00:02:23.343
Must be true beats could be true

00:02:23.623 --> 00:02:24.857
Combine two facts

00:02:25.137 --> 00:02:28.354
Watch: only, unlike, before, most

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.137
Modest beats extreme

00:02:30.687 --> 00:02:31.292
Trap

00:02:31.492 --> 00:02:33.566
Sounds smart, never proven

